{# Render-mode gate — "action" covers buy/sell/vendor drill-downs. #}
{% if render_mode == "transform" or render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "action" %}
{% if actorUUID and actorUUID != 0 and not is_player(actorUUID) %}
{% if sever_in_scene(actorUUID) == "" %}
{# Shop stock shows only while the merchant is at their shop during its hours (sever_at_shop: the vendor faction's own
   place and hours, as the game offers the barter topic; works in every language and for any merchant). #}
{% if sever_at_shop(actorUUID) != "" %}
{% set merchant_inventory = get_merchant_inventory(actorUUID) %}
{% if merchant_inventory.items and length(merchant_inventory.items) > 0 %}

## Your Shop Inventory

{% set price_multiplier = 4.5 %}
{% for item in merchant_inventory.items %}
{% set item_name = default(item.name, "") %}
{% if item_name == "" %}{% set item_name = get_form_name(item.formID) %}{% endif %}
{% if item_name != "" and item.value > 0 -%}
{% set adjusted_value = round(item.value * price_multiplier, 0) %}
- {{ item_name }}: {{ item.count }} ({{ adjusted_value }} gold)
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

## Pricing Guidelines

These are your usual asking prices. Start from them and don't volunteer discounts.
- A good customer or a bulk purchase may earn 5-15% off, and a member of your own faction 10-20%.
- If {{ player.name }} haggles, charms or leans on you and it works, you may come down by up to 20%; if it doesn't, hold firm.
- For rare items, low stock or a difficult customer, keep the price high.
- Never go below 60% of your usual price.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
